feedback.body:
I had a look at the STM32H7 datasheet: the bitmap of `CR1` and `CR2` is the same, except for one bit which we're not using and `SR1` is identical to `SR2`. We can exploit this to factor out common code like the functions unlocking the banks and performing the erase.
You can have something like
```
static inline bool unlock_bank(struct flash_cr_typedef *cr)
{
    // Flash already unlocked
    if ((*cr & FLASH_CR_LOCK) == 0) {
        return true;
    }

    FLASH->KEYR1 = 0x45670123;
    FLASH->KEYR1 = 0xCDEF89AB;
    __ISB();

    // Succesful unlock
    if ((*cr & FLASH_CR_LOCK) == 0) {
        return true;
    }

    return false;
}
```
and then call it with `unlock_bank(&FLASH->CR1)` and `unlock_bank(&FLASH->CR2)`

